n\n- **`datasette/app.py`**\n  - `__init__` adds `_setup_db_done = False` and `_startup_lock`, in both the normal and `RuntimeError` workaround branches.\n  - New `_startup_sequence()` returns early when both flags are set. Otherwise, under the lock, it runs the immutable table-count precompute if not yet done, then calls `invoke_startup()`.\n  - `app()` drops the local `setup_db`. It wraps with `AsgiLifespan(on_startup=[self._startup_sequence], on_shutdown=[_close_on_shutdown])`, then `AsgiRunOnFirstRequest(on_startup=[self._startup_sequence])`.\n- **`datasette/utils/asgi.py`**\n  - Adds `import asyncio`.\n  - `AsgiLifespan` catches startup and shutdown exceptions and sends `lifespan.startup.failed` / `lifespan.shutdown.failed` with the message.\n  - `AsgiRunOnFirstRequest` passes lifespan scopes straight through. For other scopes it takes a lock, runs the hooks, and sets `_started` only after they finish, so concurrent first requests wait for startup.\n- **`datasette/cli.py`**: `serve` calls `ds._startup_sequence()` instead of `ds.invoke_startup()`, with the comment updated.\n\nI didn't run the wider test suite beyond the two files the spec lists. I also left `SPEC.md` untracked and didn't commit anything.", "ttft_ms": 2514, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 36247, "uuid": "33c7a0b9-8261-46f5-9e58-a424d51bcedf", "ttft_stream_ms": 2235, "time_to_request_ms": 598, "first_content_frame_ms": 2235, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
